From: FP3 camera work
Subject: [PATCH] camera: restore the autofocus mode after a resolution switch

A photograph switches the source to the capture resolution and back, and
the switch reconfigures the pipeline, which brings the camera up in its
default focus mode - continuous. A photo taken with autofocus off left the
camera hunting again once the shot restored the preview. Re-apply the
viewfinder's own mode from where a switch is confirmed streaming (frames
flowing, so a control has a request to ride), which covers every
reconfiguring switch, not only the shot.
--- a/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
+++ b/aperture/src/viewfinder.rs
@@ -1974,6 +1974,13 @@
                         // does not can be sent back to.
                         imp.good_res.set(Some(imp.viewfinder_res.get()));
                         imp.switching.set(false);
+                        // The switch that brought this pipeline up also reset
+                        // the camera to its default focus mode; now that frames
+                        // are flowing to carry a control, put the mode back to
+                        // what the viewfinder should be in. Without this a photo
+                        // taken with autofocus off left the camera hunting again
+                        // once the shot's resolution switch restored the preview.
+                        obj.set_autofocus(obj.autofocus());
                         return;
                     }
 
